{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"freeborn-dizzy-raven","creation_channel":"cli","description":"Found by the evidence pass on ticket sole-curbable-stinkpot (9a71-ba9b-89d0-4cb8), which showed these runs were MISATTRIBUTED to ACLI 'command cancelled'.\n\nTwo failed Reconcile Bridge runs converged and then failed to publish, in two related-but-distinct ways:\n\n- run 31455622724 (2026-08-11T03:30Z): '! [remote rejected] 1e5caeb7 -> refs/reconciler/last-pass (failure)' -> 'ERROR: cannot publish reconciler last-pass witness: git push --force-with-lease ... returned non-zero exit status 1' -> 'Reconcile failed (exit 1)'. A stale --force-with-lease expectation on the last-pass witness ref.\n- run 31244501098 (2026-08-08T06:41Z): 'final-push-rejected: ! [remote rejected] HEAD -> tickets (cannot lock ref refs/heads/tickets: is at e45f61a9 but expected 9ecaaa40)', 6 unpushed commits. A lost race against a concurrent tickets writer.\n\nBoth are concurrency/CAS faults on publish rather than reconcile faults. The question for this ticket is whether the publish path should re-fetch and retry the CAS rather than failing the run, and whether the last-pass witness failure should be fatal at all (it is a witness, not the payload).","id":"ebee-e959-8015-4e02","parent_id":"","priority":2,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"bug","title":"Reconcile Bridge delivery fails on rejected ref pushes (stale force-with-lease + lost tickets race)"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1786517399130082001,"uuid":"1dcae2b4-4eeb-45a0-8766-97605413724e"}